      "worked": "A negative product is less than any positive product, so choose one negative and one positive number. The greatest available magnitudes of opposite signs are $7$ and $3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(-7)\\times3&=-(7\\times3)\\\\(-7)\\times3&=-21\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe least product is $-21$.",
